<%
  prompt = %{Suggest up to 5 areas for improvement for #{subject} based on the feedback below.

Further instructions (don't mention in your response):
- Present as a numbered list
- Address your answer in the second person ('you')
- Only suggest what the feedback itself points to: criticisms, suggestions, or things attendees wished were different. Don't invent any
- If the feedback points to nothing to improve, reply with just NONE

The feedback:\n\n#{feedback}}
  content = OpenRouter.chat(prompt).strip # nil (no answer) raises, as before, so nothing is cached
%>
<% if content.start_with?('NONE') || !content.include?('1.') %>
  <p>The feedback doesn't point to anything to improve.</p>
<% else %>
  <%== md(%(#{intro}:\n\n1. #{content.split('1.', 2).last.strip})) %>
<% end %>
